{"study_accession":"PRJNA1441475","secondary_study_accession":"SRP685943","title":"Activation-induced SLC7A1 expression enhances T cell sensitivity to cGAMP-mediated STING signaling [T_cells_RNA_Seq]","description":"STING agonists are promising innate immune therapies and can synergize with adaptive immune checkpoint blockade therapies for cancer treatment, but their effectiveness is limited by the toxicity to activated T cells. How STING agonists such as cGAMP and its analogs enter and induce STING activation and toxicity in T cells is unclear despite known transporters for other cell types. Here, we identify the cationic amino acid transporter SLC7A1 as a cGAMP transporter in activated primary mouse and human T cells. T cells upregulate this transporter upon activation to meet their high metabolic demand, but this comes at the cost of enabling increased transport and toxicity of cGAMP. We identified distinct residues in SLC7A1 that mediate cGAMP and arginine activity suggesting that cGAMP transport may be separable from arginine uptake. These findings suggest that modulation of SLC7A1 may influence T cell susceptibility to cGAMP and its analogs. Overall design: RNA-seq profiling of resting or stimulated (one day after four days of anti-CD3/CD28 Dynabeads) human CD3+ T cells (>99% purity) from 5 donors","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":10,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN56655512","study_accession":"PRJNA1441475","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"Human T cells donor 7, stimulated anti CD3/28","description":"Human T cells donor 7, stimulated anti CD3/28","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM9610754","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2026-05-24","attributes":[["source_name","PBMC"],["tissue","PBMC"],["cell_type","CD3+ T cells"],["treatment","day 5 post-ant-CD3/28 Dynabeads activation"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR37730661","experiment_accession":"SRX32607